## Typography

### Font families (resource keys)

| Key | Stack | Use |
|-----|--------|-----|
| `DisplayFont` | Yu Gothic UI, Meiryo UI, Segoe UI Variable Display, Segoe UI | Brand, page titles, section titles, eyebrows, DataGrid headers |
| `BodyFont` | Yu Gothic UI, Meiryo UI, Segoe UI Variable Text, Segoe UI | Body, fields, buttons, default `UserControl`/`Window` |
| `ChassisMonoFont` | Cascadia Mono, Consolas, Courier New | Chassis plates, totals, raw source monospace panes |

### Text styles (always prefer these)

| Style | Role | Notes |
|-------|------|--------|
| `BrandDisplayStyle` | Nav wordmark “CarInvoice” | ~22 Bold, SidebarText |
| `BrandEyebrowStyle` | Nav tagline | e.g. `車検証 · 和紙  ·  Invoice Desk` |
| `EyebrowStyle` | Small JP/EN certificate label | Ruri, SemiBold ~11 — above titles |
| `PageTitleStyle` | Page H1 | Display ~26 SemiBold, Sumi |
| `PageSubtitleStyle` | One-line page support | Nezumi, wrap, ~13 |
| `SectionTitleStyle` | In-card section title | Display ~16 SemiBold |
| `SectionHeaderStyle` | Alias of section title + margin | Prefer `SectionHeader` control |
| `SectionRuleStyle` | 1px hairline divider | `BorderSubtleBrush` |
| `FieldLabelStyle` | Form labels | SemiBold ~11 Nezumi; pattern `English` or `JP  ·  English` |
| `BodyTextStyle` | Long copy | Sumi, LineHeight 20 |
| `MutedTextStyle` | Meta / secondary lines | Nezumi ~12 |
| `MonoPlateStyle` | Chassis display (read-only) | Cascadia + Ruri |
| `DetailTitleStyle` | Slide-out detail make/name | Display ~20 |
| `StatusMessageStyle` | Footer status line | Nezumi ~12 |
| `BannerTextStyle` | Text inside danger/success/warning banners | SemiBold ~12.5 |
| `ToolbarCaptionStyle` | Tiny caption before toolbars | e.g. `SOURCE` |

### Label copy convention

- Eyebrows / section labels: **`日本語  ·  ENGLISH`** (middle dot `·`, thin spaces).
- Examples already in product: `伝票作成  ·  CREATE`, `車台番号  ·  CHASSIS PLATE`, `型式  ·  Chassis Code`, `顧客  ·  BUYER`, `金額  ·  PRICING`, `請求一覧  ·  LEDGER`, `用語集  ·  GLOSSARY`.
- DataGrid column headers: short **UPPERCASE English** (CODE, NUMBER, MAKE…).

## Layout components (reuse; do not reinvent)

### `Controls/PageHeader`

Properties: `Eyebrow`, `Title`, `Subtitle`.

Use at the **top of every main view**. Renders eyebrow → page title → subtitle → hairline rule.

### `Controls/SectionHeader`

Properties: `Eyebrow`, `Title`, `TrailingContent`.

Use inside cards for section breaks. Renders Ruri **left ink tick** + eyebrow + title + optional trailing (e.g. Translate button) + hairline rule.

### Surface styles

| Style | Use |
|-------|-----|
| `ChassisPlateCardStyle` | Chassis Code/Number block — Asagi fill, Ruri left border `4,1,1,1` |
| `CardSurfaceStyle` | White cards / toolbars / detail panes |
| `SuccessBadgeStyle` | Auto-lookup badge |
| `DangerBannerStyle` | Duplicate chassis alert |
| `WarningBannerStyle` | Glossary / caution callouts |
| `ChassisTextBoxStyle` | Chassis inputs only |

### Shell / navigation

- Left rail: `SidebarBackgroundBrush`, brand via `BrandDisplayStyle` + `BrandEyebrowStyle`.
- Content host: `AppBackgroundBrush` with comfortable padding (~16,12).
- Title bar: Kachi background, Sidebar text.
- Window fit: clamp to `SystemParameters.WorkArea` on startup (`MainWindow.FitToWorkingArea`) — do not hardcode oversized mins that break small screens.

## Scrolling

- Prefer **one page `ScrollViewer`** for long forms (Create Invoice). Avoid nested ScrollViewers that steal the wheel.
- Multiline TextBoxes may scroll locally only while they still have overflow; otherwise forward wheel to the page scroller (see `CreateInvoiceView`).

## Accent lock (Wpf.Ui)

Primary buttons use system accent resources. App startup **must** keep:

```csharp
ApplicationAccentColorManager.Apply(AccentAiIro, AccentAiIro, AccentAiIroHover, AccentRuriIro);
theme.SetTheme(ApplicationTheme.Light);
theme.SetAccent(AccentAiIro);
```

Never reintroduce `ApplySystemAccent()`.

## When editing UI

1. New page → start with `PageHeader`; new in-card block → `SectionHeader`.
2. New color role → add Color + Brush to `JapaneseTheme.xaml` **and** a row in the palette table above before using it.
3. Prefer `{StaticResource ...}` over leftover Wpf.Ui generic brushes for surfaces/text this theme defines.
4. Keep motion subtle if added; hierarchy comes from type + ink ticks + rules, not glow/pills/purple gradients.
